            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "The `init.lua` is as follows:\n\n```\n-- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\nvim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim\"\nlocal clone_cmd = { \"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth=1\", \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\", mini_path }\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\nvim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n-- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\nvim.cmd(\"packadd mini.nvim\")\nrequire(\"mini.deps\").setup()\n\n-- Add extra setup steps needed to reproduce the behavior\n-- Use `MiniDeps.add('user/repo')` to install another plugin from GitHub\n--\nvim.g.mapleader = vim.keycode(\"<Space>\")\n\nlocal pick = require(\"mini.pick\")\npick.setup()\n\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>ff\", pick.builtin.files, { noremap = true, silent = true, desc = \"Search files\" })\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>fb\", pick.builtin.buffers, { noremap = true, silent = true, desc = \"Search buffers\" })\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>fs\", pick.builtin.grep_live, { noremap = true, silent = true, desc = \"Search text\" })\n```\n\nI'm using the clean config as described.\n\nThe problem happens whether the file is nested or not, and using `:Pick files` also generates the same error. `:Pick buffers` and `:Pick grep_live` work normally.\n\nThis file structure:\n\n```\n.\n├── coração.md\n├── init.lua\n└── test\n    └── coração.md\n```\n\nGenerates this:\n\n<img width=\"959\" height=\"1050\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ad08a6ea-3342-4086-945d-b4b1f01474a5\" />",
