            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> The `init.lua` is as follows:\n\nThe important note here is that you don't have `rg` or `fd` installed and are using 'git' as a too *and* this is inside a Git repol. Running `:Pick files tool='git'` indeed reproduces this for me.\n\nThis happens because `git ls-files --cached --others` returns this kind of output:\n\n```\n\"cora\\303\\247\\303\\243o.md\"\ninit.lua\n\"test/cora\\303\\247\\303\\243o.md\"\n```\n\nI'll take a look if there needs to be an extra care done for the `'git'` tool. But in the meantime I'd highly recommend installing `ripgrep` CLI tool, as it works as expected here and is generally faster.\n\nOr configure Git with the following `git config --global core.quotepath false`.",
